   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Loss of the umlaut and regularity",
     "texto": [
      "All modal verbs in the Präteritum are conjugated with the stem without umlaut and the past ending: **konnte** (could), **musste** (had to), **durfte** (was allowed), **wollte** (wanted), **sollte** (was supposed to).",
      "As with «sein» and «haben», the 1st and 3rd person singular are identical: **ich konnte / er konnte**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Differences in meaning",
     "texto": [
      "**Durfte** expresses that someone had permission or authorisation; with negation (**durfte nicht**) it means a firm prohibition in the past. **Musste** denotes an unavoidable obligation, whereas **konnte** indicates physical or intellectual ability or possibility."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
